<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBP-F011>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBP-F011" ;
  triage:title "DecisionSchema is a new public trait in a published crate with no explicit open-or-sealed decision" ;
  triage:description "DecisionSchema is a new public trait in a published crate with no explicit open-or-sealed decision. D5 says new variants are added inside this crate (a SchemaFamily variant, a module and a schema_for arm), so the implementor set is crate-controlled. External implementations would be unusable anyway, since schema_for cannot reach them. Recommendation: Seal it with the private supertrait pattern, or make it pub(crate) until a second variant exists, and document the decision. JudgeBackend stays intentionally open (ADR-SAG-0009); say so in its doc." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-a-refine" ;
